  "id": "COMPOUND:33280 - PROTEIN:5858",
  "verbalization": "Sarcotrine A is shown to have targets that ultimately lead to KB through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Sarcotrine A interacts with Hepatocyte, which in turn is targeted by Cocosamide B and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. These compounds all have a shared relationship with KB, indicating a potential pathway where Sarcotrine A's effects are mediated through these intermediates. The presence of multiple targets for Sarcotrine A, each of which is linked to KB, suggests a broader mechanism of action that may involve the modulation of cellular processes in hepatocytes. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Sarcotrine A in influencing cellular targets that ultimately converge on KB, reinforcing the notion of a complex, interconnected network of molecular interactions.",
